# Keep the build context to the sources the image actually needs.
#
# Without this file the context was ~1.9 GB and every build shipped the host's
# node_modules into the daemon. That is not merely slow: the Dockerfile installs
# dependencies with `npm ci` and only THEN runs `COPY frontend/ ./`, so the
# host's tree was copied straight over the freshly installed one. The image was
# built against whatever happened to be on the build machine rather than against
# package-lock.json — and on a 40 GB disk the copy is what ran the filesystem
# out of space mid-build.
#
# NOTHING here may exclude runtime data. `backend/data/` carries the vendored
# marnet graph, the land mask and the Natural Earth country outlines, and the
# production image needs all three — without marnet.geojson the sea router
# throws ENOENT on the first cruise request, and without countries-10m.geojson
# the point-to-country lookup throws on the first location-history sweep.
#
# Watch the `**/*.test.ts` and `**/__tests__` rules below in particular: a
# pattern written to exclude tests will happily exclude a data file that
# happens to sit under a matching name. `backend/data/` holds none today; keep
# it that way.

# Installed dependencies — always reinstalled inside the image from the lockfile
**/node_modules

# Version control and local agent state
.git
.gitignore
.claude
.roadmap

# Build output — the image builds its own
frontend/dist
backend/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Local runtime state that must never be baked into an image
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
backend/.travstats-data
data/logs
**/*.log

# Test and development material
e2e
test-samples
**/coverage
**/__tests__
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
playwright-report
test-results

# Documentation and tooling that no runtime path reads
docs
tools
.github
